<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN POST OFFICE WANTS TO RUN LOTTERY.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN POST OFFICE WANTS TO RUN LOTTERY.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's post office will tender to run the country's planned national lottery which is due to be in place by the second half of next year, Telecommunications Minister Jay Naidoo said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, we are vying for the licence to run the national state lottery,&quot; Naidoo told parliament in reply to a member's question.</p>
<p>&quot;Lotteries in most part of the world are run by the state, and run by post offices,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The department of trade and industry said earlier this month that tenders would be invited to run the lottery.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town parliamentary office +27 21 403-2502</p>
</text>
